fixed on me with unseen focus  of a mind as alien to mine as a deep-sea  worm I stood frozen and uncomprehending  as it slowly strode forward its wheezing  body barely bigger than that of a child  its glaring eyes were fixed on me the  puppy thing slowly drawing closer I  could not move dirt read would result  only an eventual captured by the thing  but to advance would mean crossing it  and the thought of touching that thing  the decision was made for me for is the  thing drew close I was galvanized into  action by horror or rage I left forward  screaming nonsense and struck at that  bloated body I kicked and stumped at it  crushing the flabby and far too soft  flesh underneath me sobbing in horror as  I felt the flesh touched me  then melt away rotting to nothingness in  seconds believing such an unclean memory  in me that I knew I would feel that dull  soggy weight against me long after even  the sweet cold embrace him beyond after  that I ran I ran and cursed whatever  blind faded brought me here an  obliteration my memory my life and left  only the road  we had terminal Road I would have cried  I've balled up and throw myself down one  of the analyst pits that broken open the  road but I was compelled to continue  legs continuing in a jerky rhythm that  propelled me over the crumbling brick  leaping across the pits  even as I secretly wished to fall into  their depths and obliterate the road the  faces and myself as I ran and jumped I  came to one of the thick twisted tubes  that dotted the claustrophobic landscape  I thought to look in for a moment  curiosity fighting to overcome my almost  manic desire to be free of this place  but upon hearing a strange shuffling and  gurgling coupled with a deep bass pulse  from the bowels of the black pipe I  decided against it squeezed it round as  soon as I was passed there was a sudden  rush of air behind me followed by a  sharp oddly muffled snap as if two iron  bars wrapped in Conda be thrown together  behind me I did not turn merely using  this to further galvanize my stuttering  walk ignoring that continued snapping  and rustling as it faded behind me far  ahead I saw long glassy stare leading up  and beyond it would look like a squat  dwelling made of the same crumbling  brick as the road while I feared what  may lie inside the idea of someone else  some other person with which to share  this horrible place with filled me with  the first hope I felt in hours I ran  eyes fixed on that stare and soared  across the final gap  it was midway across the abyss when I  saw the thing was waiting on the other  side it was a twisted parody of some  kind of a reptile its elongated face was  filled with a dim sort of Menace and his  mouth yawned in anticipation of my  reaching the other side the jagged edge  is glinting as I made a choking squeal  its body balanced on to squat shapeless  legs a shell hard cracked flesh encasing  the bulbous torso two stunted limbs  projected through the flaking shale  coated in fibrous growths and slowly  shifted and a sick mockery of wings I  screamed and twisted trying in vain to  return to the far edge but it was too  late then my struggles were enough to  bring me short slamming into the hard  wall of the pit nothing above me  shrieking in frustration as I fell down  and down spinning into the endless  blackness I felt the dark and clothes  around me  however seconds before the emptiness can  provide me a final solace I suddenly  remembered endless roads Lake Sapphire  crumbling tombs filled with rotting  shambling bones of beasts hazy forms of  glowing slickly light following in the  dark  floating networks of ancient wood  drifting in a hot sky it all came back  to me in a flood then remembered  somewhere I had been what I had done and  knowing that it would continue I do not  know how long I have done this nor what  I have done to earn this  only that I must walk the road forever  you
 

